Example 4:

10
00:01:47,047 --> 00:02:02,391
Calculate then compare value of (a + b) + c and a + (b + c).

11
00:02:03,884 --> 00:02:18,294
We have: a = 2.5; b = 6.8; c = 1.2.

12
00:02:20,058 --> 00:02:31,967
Calculate: a + b = 2.5 + 6.8 = 9.3.

13
00:02:32,765 --> 00:02:46,880
(a + b) + c = 9.3 + 1.2 = 10.5.

14
00:02:47,958 --> 00:02:59,086
(b + c) = 6.8 + 1.2 = 8.

15
00:03:00,925 --> 00:03:13,918
a + (b + c) = 2.5 + 8 = 10.5.

16
00:03:15,884 --> 00:03:31,536
So: (a + b) + c = a + (b + c) = 10.5.

17
00:03:34,984 --> 00:03:36,555
Conclusion:

18
00:03:36,872 --> 00:04:12,032
Addition has associative property: When adding a sum of two numbers with third number, we can add first number with sum of two remaining numbers.

